# Frontend environment variables.
#
# Copy to .env.local (Git-ignored) if you need to override anything:
#
#   cp .env.example .env.local
#
# Local development needs no variables at all. The app calls the API with
# relative paths and Vite proxies /api/** and /media/** to the backend on
# http://localhost:8081 (see vite.config.ts), so just start Spring Boot first.
#
# Only variables prefixed with VITE_ are exposed to client code, and they are
# inlined into the bundle at build time — never put secrets here.

# Reserved for pointing the app at an API that is not behind the dev proxy.
# Nothing reads this yet: the code has no import.meta.env usage, so setting it
# has no effect until a base-URL lookup is added to src/shared/api/client.ts.
# VITE_API_BASE_URL='https://api.example.com'
